   },
   "evidence": "src/util/proc.ts:873-875 records `directory = realpathSync(directory)` in each discovery row. At head, the lookups use the raw request cwd: workers.ts:372 `const { cwd } = JSON.parse(job.request)` then `listProcessDiscoveries(undefined, cwd)`; inplace.ts:77 `!store.listProcessDiscoveries(undefined, req.cwd).length && ... -> stopped=1`; lan.ts:55 `json_extract(request,'$.cwd')=?` with the raw spelling. Store.listProcessDiscoveries matches by exact string or prefix only. Default production paths (~/.limitless/work under /Users) are usually canonical, so the bypass needs a symlinked path. The reviewer's claim that these tests fail on Linux CI is doubtful, since /tmp is already canonical there."
