   },
   "evidence": "The probe used real gate subprocesses and retryBaselineFailures with fake confinement. Setup wrote `$HOME/setup-token`; the check required that token and deliberately failed its first attempt. Local execution shared an outer withCommandScratch scope and passed its retry; actual in-place executor jobs did not. Each executor job calls executeGate independently at HEAD, and runLocalGates creates/removes scratch around that call. Meanwhile `freshCheckoutFor: (repo) => !inplace && repos.includes(repo)` makes retryFailures select `setup: []`. At base, in-process attempts share the pipeline command scope, and configured LAN retries rerun setup."
  }
